# Line-ending policy for this artifact release.
#
# Without this file, `core.autocrlf=true` (a common global default on Windows) rewrites
# LF to CRLF on checkout.  That changes file *bytes* without changing Git content, so
# `RELEASE_SHA256SUMS.txt` / `RELEASE_MANIFEST.json` verification fails for every text
# file even though nothing is actually wrong.  In the pre-publication rehearsal this hit
# 633 of 2079 files on a machine with a global autocrlf=true.
#
# The manifests in this repository are byte-exact and line-ending sensitive, so the
# checkout must be byte-exact too, on every platform.  Therefore: pin LF everywhere
# except the formats that require CRLF by specification.
#
# Git normalises to LF in the object database; `eol=lf` additionally guarantees LF in the
# working tree regardless of core.autocrlf.

* text=auto eol=lf

# --- binary (never touch) ---
*.npz   binary
*.zip   binary
*.docx  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary

# --- explicit text, LF in the working tree ---
*.py      text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.txt     text eol=lf
*.csv     text eol=lf
*.tsv     text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.toml    text eol=lf
*.cff     text eol=lf
*.cfg     text eol=lf
*.ini     text eol=lf
*.ps1     text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.tex     text eol=lf
*.bib     text eol=lf
*.jsonl   text eol=lf
*.patch   text eol=lf
*.diff    text eol=lf
*.log     text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf

# --- CRLF by specification ---
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf

# --- mis-extensioned captures: byte-exact, never transformed ---
# Two captured console transcripts are not UTF-8/ASCII despite their extensions; they carry
# NUL bytes (UTF-16 text and interleaved padding).  Git must not normalise or re-encode them,
# so they are marked explicitly non-text.  Their manifests hash the bytes as shipped.
audit/risk_field/07_stdout.txt                 -text
scripts/_run_m1_solver_ablation_orig.py        -text

# --- HASH-LOCKED TREES: byte-exact, never normalised ---
#
# These trees are cryptographically pinned.  config/locked_spec.json,
# config/FROZEN_PROTOCOL_MANIFEST.json and MANIFEST.json record the SHA256 of specific
# artifact bytes, and the R7 executor and independent validator refuse to run when those
# bytes differ.  Line-ending normalisation is therefore a *correctness* hazard here, not a
# style choice: converting these files CRLF->LF changed locked_spec.json from
# 9775479b... to c478a6ab... and turned GATE_E from PASS into FAIL.
#
# They must keep their original bytes on checkout, on every platform, whatever the host's
# core.autocrlf setting is.  Marking them binary (-text) disables all EOL conversion and
# diff textconv for them.
out/r7_confirmatory_kernel_ranking_20260917/**  -text
out/handoff_r11_remaining6/**                   -text
out/r5_posthoc_hparam_sensitivity_20260917/**   -text
out/r6_posthoc_kernel_k_control_20260917/**     -text
audit/risk_field/**                             -text


